<title>FRANCE: Thomson, Dasa in helicopter radar offer.</title>
<headline>Thomson, Dasa in helicopter radar offer.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF said on Saturday it has made a joint offer with Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG and FIAR of Italy, to supply a naval radar for the NH90 military helicopter.</p>
<p>The three firms are proposing the Tactical Radar Subsystem European Navy Radar for the NH90 anti-submarine version. &quot;Based on the proposal submitted by the ENR partners, NHI recommended the selection of this radar to the participating governments,&quot; Thomson-CSF said in a statement at the Paris air show.</p>
<p>NH Industries is the prime contractor for the NH90, which is being built for France, Germany, Italy and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>FIAR is a unit of industrial holding company Finmeccanica .</p>
<p>Eurocopter, a joint venture between French state-owned Aerospatiale and Daimler-Benz Aerospace, Agusta Spa of Italy and Fokker Aviation of the Netherlands are building the NH90.</p>
<p>-- Pierre Tran, Le Bourget newsroom +33 1 4169 3650. pnt</p>
